+The remaining change types (`synthesis`, `attestation`, `restoration`, `format conversion`) are not applicable to these direct methods, so they contradict every one of them and a server SHOULD reject them with `400 Bad Request` as well; VERSIONs with such a `change_type` are committed through the CONTRIBUTION endpoint, where the audit details are supplied explicitly.
 
 The list of `code_string` values and their meaning is specified by the [Audit Change Type](https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/TERM/latest/SupportTerminology.html#_audit_change_type) and [Version Lifecycle State](https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/TERM/latest/SupportTerminology.html#_version_lifecycle_state) openEHR terminology vocabularies.
 
